<%- include('../../partials/header') %>
<main id="main-content" class="container">
  <div class="calculator-header">
    <h1>North Carolina Closing Cost Calculator (<%= currentYear %>)</h1>
    <p class="lead-description">
      Calculate buyer and seller settlement costs across North Carolina. Includes the <strong>NC Excise Stamp Tax ($2 per $1,000)</strong>, Due Diligence fee accounting, mandatory closing attorney fees, and regulated title insurance rates.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="calculator-layout">
    <!-- LEFT INPUT PANEL -->
    <div class="calculator-panel">
      <h2 class="panel-title">North Carolina Property &amp; Contract Details</h2>

      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="ncPrice">Property Purchase Price ($):</label>
        <input type="number" id="ncPrice" class="form-control" value="395000" min="20000" step="5000">
        <span class="field-hint">Charlotte &amp; Raleigh median residential sales benchmark.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="ncRole">Your Transaction Role:</label>
        <select id="ncRole" class="form-control">
          <option value="buyer" selected>Buyer (Purchasing Home)</option>
          <option value="seller">Seller (Selling Home)</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="form-group" id="groupNcDown">
        <label for="ncDownPct">Buyer Down Payment (%):</label>
        <select id="ncDownPct" class="form-control">
          <option value="5">5% Down Payment</option>
          <option value="10">10% Down Payment</option>
          <option value="20" selected>20% Down Payment (Standard)</option>
          <option value="0">Cash Purchase (0% Financing)</option>
        </select>
      </div>

      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="ncDueDiligence">Due Diligence Fee Paid Upfront ($):</label>
        <input type="number" id="ncDueDiligence" class="form-control" value="4000" min="0" step="500">
        <span class="field-hint">Non-refundable fee credited toward purchase price at closing.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="form-group" id="groupNcComm" style="display:none;">
        <label for="ncAgentComm">Real Estate Broker Commission (%):</label>
        <input type="number" id="ncAgentComm" class="form-control" value="5.0" min="0" max="8.0" step="0.5">
      </div>

      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="ncAttorney">Closing Attorney Fee ($):</label>
        <input type="number" id="ncAttorney" class="form-control" value="900" min="0" step="50">
        <span class="field-hint">Mandatory closing attorney in NC ($750&ndash;$1,200).</span>
      </div>

      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="ncAnnualTax">Annual Property Taxes ($):</label>
        <input type="number" id="ncAnnualTax" class="form-control" value="3150" min="0" step="100">
        <span class="field-hint">Average NC effective property tax rate (~0.80%&ndash;0.95%).</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- RIGHT RESULTS PANEL -->
    <div class="calculator-panel results-panel">
      <h2 class="panel-title">Your Estimated NC Settlement Summary</h2>

      <div class="highlight-metric">
        <div class="metric-label" id="resNcRoleLabel">Total Buyer Closing Costs</div>
        <div class="metric-value primary-value" id="resNcTotalCost">$0</div>
        <div class="metric-sub" id="resNcBottomLine">Estimated Cash Needed at Settlement: $0</div>
      </div>

      <div class="results-grid">
        <div class="result-card">
          <div class="result-title" id="resNcCard1Title">Due Diligence Credit</div>
          <div class="result-number text-success" id="resNcCard1Val">-$4,000</div>
          <div class="result-desc" id="resNcCard1Desc">Credited against cash-to-close</div>
        </div>

        <div class="result-card">
          <div class="result-title">Title Insurance (Lender &amp; Owner)</div>
          <div class="result-number" id="resNcTitleFees">$0</div>
          <div class="result-desc">Regulated NC title policy</div>
        </div>

        <div class="result-card">
          <div class="result-title">Closing Attorney &amp; Recording</div>
          <div class="result-number" id="resNcAttorneyRecording">$0</div>
          <div class="result-desc">Legal counsel + County deed recording</div>
        </div>

        <div class="result-card">
          <div class="result-title" id="resNcCard4Title">Lender &amp; Escrow Prepaids</div>
          <div class="result-number" id="resNcCard4Val">$0</div>
          <div class="result-desc" id="resNcCard4Desc">Taxes &amp; Insurance Buffer</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="summary-breakdown">
        <h3>Itemized North Carolina Settlement Statement</h3>
        <table class="summary-table">
          <tr><td>Home Purchase Price:</td><td id="resSumNcPrice">$0</td></tr>
          <tr id="rowNcDown"><td>Buyer Down Payment:</td><td id="resSumNcDown">$0</td></tr>
          <tr id="rowNcComm" style="display:none;"><td>Broker Commission (5%):</td><td id="resSumNcComm">$0</td></tr>
          <tr><td>NC Excise Stamp Tax ($2.00/$1k):</td><td id="resSumNcExcise">$0</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Title Insurance Policy:</td><td id="resSumNcTitle">$0</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Closing Attorney Legal Fee:</td><td id="resSumNcAttorney">$0</td></tr>
          <tr id="rowNcEscrow"><td>Escrow Prepaids (Taxes &amp; Insurance):</td><td id="resSumNcEscrow">$0</td></tr>
          <tr id="rowNcDdCredit"><td>Less Due Diligence Fee Paid Upfront:</td><td class="text-success" id="resSumNcDdCredit">-$0</td></tr>
          <tr class="highlight-row"><td><strong id="resSumNcFinalLabel">Total Remaining Cash to Close:</strong></td><td><strong id="resSumNcFinalVal">$0</strong></td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- CONTENT & GUIDES -->
  <div class="calculator-content-body">
    <div class="quick-answer-card">
      <h2>How North Carolina Real Estate Closing Costs Work in <%= currentYear %></h2>
      <p>
        In North Carolina, buyer closing costs average <strong>2.0% to 3.5%</strong> when financing, while seller closing costs average <strong>6.0% to 8.0%</strong>. North Carolina operates as an <strong>attorney closing state</strong> and features a distinctive <strong>Due Diligence Fee contract mechanism</strong> alongside the state <strong>Real Estate Excise Stamp Tax ($2.00 per $1,000 paid by the seller)</strong>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>The North Carolina Due Diligence Fee Mechanism Explained</h2>
    <p>
      In North Carolina standard Offer to Purchase and Contract (Form 2-T), buyers provide a <strong>Due Diligence Fee</strong> directly to the seller upon signing:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Non-Refundable Right to Terminate:</strong> The fee buys the buyer an agreed time period (typically 2 to 4 weeks) to inspect the property, secure financing, conduct appraisals, and terminate for any reason.</li>
      <li><strong>100% Credited at Closing:</strong> If the transaction proceeds to closing, 100% of the Due Diligence Fee is credited directly toward the purchase price and reduces the buyer's remaining cash needed at the settlement table.</li>
    </ul>

